            <p id="d1e1939-35-1" class="oj-ti-grseq-1">
               <span class="oj-italic">Guidance on how to calculate and report land<span class="oj-bold">-use</span>
               </span>
            </p>
            <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
               <col width="4%"/>
               <col width="4%"/>
               <col width="92%"/>
               <tbody>
                  <tr>
                     <td valign="top"  />
                     <td valign="top"  >
                        <p class="oj-normal">74.</p>
                     </td>
                     <td valign="top"  >
                        <span>A <span class="oj-bold">
                              <span class="oj-italic">
                              ‘sealed area’
                           </span>
                           </span> is to be understood as an area where the original soil has been covered (e.g. roads, buildings, parking lots), making it impermeable and resulting in an <span class="oj-bold">
                              <span class="oj-italic">impact</span>
                           </span> on the environment.</span>
                     </td>
                  </tr>
               </tbody>
            </table>
            <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
               <col width="4%"/>
               <col width="4%"/>
               <col width="92%"/>
               <tbody>
                  <tr>
                     <td valign="top"  />
                     <td valign="top"  >
                        <p class="oj-normal">75.</p>
                     </td>
                     <td valign="top"  >
                        <span>Green area or ‘<span class="oj-bold">
                              <span class="oj-italic">nature-oriented area</span>
