                     <td valign="top"  >
                        <p class="oj-normal">142.</p>
                     </td>
                     <td valign="top"  >
                        <span>Under paragraph 43, the undertaking shall report on the total number of convictions and the total amount of fines incurred for violating anti-<span class="oj-bold">
                              <span class="oj-italic">corruption</span>
                           </span> and anti-<span class="oj-bold">
                              <span class="oj-italic">bribery</span>
                           </span> laws.</span>
                     </td>
                  </tr>
               </tbody>
            </table>
            <p id="d1e3822-35-1" class="oj-ti-grseq-1">
               <span class="oj-italic">Guidance on convictions</span>
            </p>
            <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
               <col width="4%"/>
               <col width="4%"/>
               <col width="92%"/>
               <tbody>
                  <tr>
                     <td valign="top"  />
                     <td valign="top"  >
                        <p class="oj-normal">143.</p>
                     </td>
                     <td valign="top"  >
                        <span>Convictions for the violation of anti-<span class="oj-bold">
                              <span class="oj-italic">corruption</span>
                           </span> and anti-<span class="oj-bold">
                              <span class="oj-italic">bribery</span>
                           </span> laws refer to any verdict of a criminal court against an individual or undertaking in respect of a criminal offence related to corruption and bribery, for example where these court decisions are entered in the criminal record of the convicting European Union Member State.</span>
                     </td>
                  </tr>
               </tbody>
